[
  {
    "id": "hack_s1",
    "text": [
      {
        "id": "s1_title",
        "text": "Which fusion is worth testing?\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s1_team",
        "text": "TEAM FUSION    Chris Paton \u00b7 Nathan Ewer \u00b7 Amber Wu \u00b7 Eva Klemencic \u00b7 Sasha Cheparukhin\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s1_tag",
        "text": "Team Fusion turns scattered chimeric-RNA evidence into a source-linked next experiment.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s1_problem_h",
        "text": "THE PROBLEM\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s1_problem",
        "text": "A ranked gene pair is not yet an exact RNA junction\u2014or a functional protein.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s1_approach_h",
        "text": "OUR APPROACH\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s1_approach",
        "text": "Trace each claim to reads, probes, structures and the paper. Let the evidence determine the next check.\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "fusion_ladder",
    "text": [
      {
        "id": "fusion_ladder_s2_title",
        "text": "RNA, junction, protein: separate the proof\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_ladder_g409e190953d_1_0",
        "text": "Reported RNA support is a starting point. Each next claim needs its own evidence.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_h0",
        "text": "01  RNA PAIR\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_b0",
        "text": "Do these genes\nappear together?\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_c0",
        "text": "109 reported\nNanoString-supported pairs\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_arrow0",
        "text": "\u2192\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_h1",
        "text": "02  EXACT JUNCTION\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_b1",
        "text": "Where do the two\nsequences join?\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_c1",
        "text": "Read alignments +\nprobe coordinates\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_arrow1",
        "text": "\u2192\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_h2",
        "text": "03  PROTEIN\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_b2",
        "text": "Is it translated\nand functional?\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_c2",
        "text": "Protein and functional\nexperiments\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lad_note",
        "text": "One evidence layer cannot stand in for the next.\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "hack_s2",
    "text": [
      {
        "id": "s2_title",
        "text": "From candidate to scientist review\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "g409e190953d_1_0",
        "text": "Codex executed 12 bounded tool calls across three cases on Brev. Every recorded output replays exactly.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "wf_inputs_h",
        "text": "PUBLISHED EVIDENCE\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "wf_inputs_b",
        "text": "Reads and probes\nPaper passages\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "wf_agent_h",
        "text": "CODEX + CPU TOOLS\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "wf_agent_b",
        "text": "Choose a check\nInspect the result\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "wf_scientist_h",
        "text": "SCIENTIST\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "wf_scientist_b",
        "text": "Review next step\nRevise or defer\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "wf_nvidia_h",
        "text": "NVIDIA PARABRICKS / A100\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "wf_nvidia_b",
        "text": "2M short-read pairs; real output\nrechecked for exact junction support\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "hack_s3",
    "text": [
      {
        "id": "s3_title",
        "text": "924 bases change the next question\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3_evidence_h",
        "text": "EVIDENCE\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3_evidence",
        "text": "Six published read IDs.\nThe nearest endpoint still differs.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3_use_h",
        "text": "NEXT ACTION\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3_use",
        "text": "Inspect the source alignment before selecting the junction assay.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3_limit_h",
        "text": "WHAT THIS MEANS\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3_limit",
        "text": "A discrepancy to resolve;\nnot proof of false RNA.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "case_name",
        "text": "Psap\u2013Lgals3\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "case_source",
        "text": "Direct source audit: Supplementary Tables 3/8 + GENCODE M28.\nDescriptive discrepancy; long-read coordinate convention is unresolved.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "gap_num",
        "text": "924 bases\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "gap_desc",
        "text": "Genomic endpoint discrepancy\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "gap_read",
        "text": "Nearest read\n47,622,058\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "gap_probe",
        "text": "Probe\n47,622,982\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "fusion_protein",
    "text": [
      {
        "id": "fusion_protein_s3_title",
        "text": "A model is one layer of evidence\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_protein_s3_evidence_h",
        "text": "PUBLISHED EVIDENCE\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_protein_s3_evidence",
        "text": "Gsdmd\u2013Tmem106a has protein and functional experiments in the paper.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_protein_s3_use_h",
        "text": "OUR MODEL\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_protein_s3_use",
        "text": "118-aa reference hypothesis.\nMean pLDDT 48.7.\nLow confidence.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_protein_s3_limit_h",
        "text": "INTERPRETATION\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_protein_s3_limit",
        "text": "Model uncertainty does not refute the experiments.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "protein_caption",
        "text": "Gsdmd\u2013Tmem106a \u00b7 reference hypothesis\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "protein_source",
        "text": "Model: Boltz2 2.2.1. Colours show parent segments, not confidence.\nExperimental context: Venezia et al., Nature (2026), Figs 3\u20134.\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "fusion_eval",
    "text": [
      {
        "id": "fusion_eval_s3_title",
        "text": "Does Hi-C improve the ranking?\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_eval_s3_evidence_h",
        "text": "MATCHED EVALUATION\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_eval_s3_evidence",
        "text": "401 pairs with complete Hi-C.\nFive gene-disjoint folds.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_eval_s3_use_h",
        "text": "UNCERTAINTY\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_eval_s3_use",
        "text": "\u0394AP: +0.004\n95% interval:\n\u22120.031 to +0.047\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_eval_s3_limit_h",
        "text": "CONCLUSION\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_eval_s3_limit",
        "text": "No established gain.\nAssay support is the label.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "ap_head",
        "text": "Held-out average precision\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "ap_label0",
        "text": "RNA features\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "ap_value0",
        "text": "0.296\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "ap_label1",
        "text": "RNA + Hi-C\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "ap_value1",
        "text": "0.300\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "ap_zero",
        "text": "0\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "ap_one",
        "text": "1\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "ap_source",
        "text": "Same 401-pair cohort; interval resamples gene components.\nUnreported NanoString support is not a verified negative.\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "fusion_close",
    "text": [
      {
        "id": "fusion_close_s1_title",
        "text": "Make the next experiment defensible.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_close_s1_team",
        "text": "TEAM FUSION    Source-linked evidence review for chimeric RNA\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_close_s1_tag",
        "text": "A visible chain from the scientific claim to the evidence\u2014and the next decision.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_close_s1_problem_h",
        "text": "DELIVERED\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_close_s1_problem",
        "text": "3 reviewed cases\n12 exact tool replays\n30 passing tests\nPublic reproducible release\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_close_s1_approach_h",
        "text": "NEXT VALIDATION\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "fusion_close_s1_approach",
        "text": "Resolve source alignments.\nTest with independent scientists.\nMeasure whether review improves decisions.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "closing_repo",
        "text": "github.com/cheparukhin/team-fusion-hackathon\n"
      }
    ]
  },
